From 806160ec5e2528317888f838a6578d356559dd95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:45:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sx8): recover the S-X8 v4.3 PCA correction that GGUF
 conversion drops (lane-242/R53)

Every 30-byte S-X8 block carries two signed-4-bit PCA coefficients, but the PCA bases and
scales live only in the .sx8v43 container. The author's GGUF converter drops them and his
llama.cpp patch ignores the coefficients. This recovers both halves and measures what they
are worth.

  tools/sx8/extract_sx8_pca.py     bases/scales out of a container over HTTP RANGE requests,
                                   skipping every block payload: 300 MB read of the 4.38 GB
                                   4B file, 550 MB of the 26.09 GB 27B file, both landing on
                                   exact EOF. --verify-stream re-reads the whole container
                                   with the reference reader and proves the walk bit-identical
                                   without putting 4.38 GB on disk.
  tools/sx8/add_sx8_pca_to_gguf.py writes them, with the coefficient planes unpacked from the
                                   blocks already in the GGUF, into a companion GGUF: 366 MB
                                   beside the 4B instead of a 3.9 GB model rewrite, and no
                                   26 GB rewrite for the 27B at all.
  loader                           picks the companion up as an extra file, so its tensors take
                                   the ordinary weights_map / backend-upload route.
  build_lora_mm                    applies Y[n] += c0*Z0 + c1*Z1 in stock ggml ops, so CPU,
                                   Vulkan and any future backend share one implementation and
                                   no kernel or shader learns about PCA.

Absent a companion the map is empty and the graph is the pre-R53 graph, bit for bit.

The correction is right and it is small. Against float64 goldens taken from the spec it lands
within 7.3e-07 of the output on CPU and 4.3e-08 on Vulkan, the two backends agree to 8.2e-07,
and a planted coefficient-sign flip is caught. In weight space it moves five tested tensors
TOWARD a Q8_0 reference by 3.0-3.4% RMS error, while a sign flip and a c0/c1 swap both move
them away. But PPL wikitext-2 on the 4B goes 9.9989 -> 9.9955, -0.034%, against the -2.64% of
the author's Table 4. On this file the dropped PCA coefficients are worth ~0.03% of perplexity,
not the 2.6% gap. See OPUS-R53-SX8-PCA-REPORT.md section 6 for what reproduces and what does not.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-242 R53 S-X8 PCA correction path, Opus 5 MEDIUM maker; formula and bases from MarlaLabs S-X8 v4.3, Apache-2.0)
Measured-effect: QUALITY - PPL wikitext-2 4B S-X8 9.9989 -> 9.9955 (-0.034%) with PCA ON (Q8_0 9.9742); llama-perplexity -c 512, 580 chunks, one cell at a time; speed UNMEASURED
Lane: lane-242
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
